## Original Content
Over the years, you’ve probably heard at least a few people casually describe themselves as Epicureans. As used today, the label can refer to as little as enjoying the occasional expensive restaurant meal. The bar was a bit higher in the second century, as explained by ancient-history YouTuber Garrett Ryan in the new video above [&#8230;]

## Summary
The article explores Epicureanism, an ancient philosophy often misunderstood in modern times as merely enjoying luxury. It references historical explanations by YouTuber Garrett Ryan, highlighting the difference between contemporary and ancient perceptions of the philosophy.

## Key Points
- Epicureanism is a controversial ancient philosophy.
- Modern usage of 'Epicurean' typically refers to enjoying fine dining or luxury.
- Historically, in the second century, Epicureanism involved stricter principles.
- Garrett Ryan, an ancient-history YouTuber, provides context in a video.


